From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:14:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: core DMA, tx path and MMIO

83 KUnit tests in 5 suites. In-scope coverage:
- dma.c: 0% -> 97.0%
- tx.c: 4.1% -> 76.5%
- mmio.c: 18.3% -> 100%

- mt76-dma, mt76-dma-rx, mt76-dma-wed: real rings in coherent DMA memory,
  with the queue registers in a buffer the test plays the hardware for.
  - queue alloc and reset (EMI, and the dead-bus clamp);
  - txwi/rxwi caches;
  - tx_queue_skb: linear and fragmented frames, the 32-buffer limit, a
    full queue, reset, prepare errors and the 4-byte pad;
  - raw tx and tx cleanup;
  - rx fill and process: budget, drop flags, fragments, oversized frames;
  - WED rx tokens and the WED-RRO rings, including the fork's
    repeat/old/unknown-token fixes;
  - NAPI poll, init and cleanup.
- mt76-tx: recording queue ops, with the tx worker parked.
  - the pending and off-channel lists, and schedule_pending ordering and
    hold-back, including the stranded-frames requeue fix;
  - the tx worker across phys;
  - non-AQL accounting on the primary link (the MLO fixes);
  - tx-status pktids, including the stale-entry check;
  - completion ordering and the timeout sweep;
  - powersave transitions and the U-APSD EOSP;
  - tokens and rx tokens.
- mt76-mmio: the bus ops, copies with odd tails, register pairs and the
  irq mask.

Not covered: tx.c's mac80211 TXQ dequeue and scheduling loop. That needs
mac80211 txqs, which only exist on interfaces created from userspace. The
VM's hwsim self-test runs that path end to end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
